  previous text: No Siebel Mobile – This feature allows data synchronization for the • Siebel Mobile No Automatic Data mobile user to happen in the background Guide: Synchronization automatically with minimal user intervention. This Disconnected improves mobile user experience. Some of the salient features are:
  current text: - System Administrator can set the frequency for auto-synchronization based on usage patterns. - • Any data created in the offline application will get synchronized automatically as soon as the user goes online. - • The user’s database gets synchronized automatically when the user is working online ensuring that user always have the latest data, whenever they go offline. - • Automatic Data Synchronization feature comes as part of Siebel Mobile Disconnected. - • Fast performance, since automatic data synchronization applies to incremental data only, the number of transactions created by the user when they were offline isn’t likely to be large. In addition, synchronization happens via a separate thread which takes care of synchronization in the background and doesn’t affect usability.
